## ApacheCon Europe 2000's Premier Sponsors

![[]Covalent Technologies](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/covalent_135x50.gif)

[[]Covalent Technologies](http://www.covalent.net/)

**Premier Sponsor**

**Expo Welcoming Reception**

**Coffee Mug**

Covalent Technologies is the leader in e-commerce solutions and
secured data applications for the Apache Web server platform. Covalent
develops commercial software enhancements for Apache, including
several plug in security and management modules, and is the only source
for comprehensive commercial support for the Apache Web server
platform.

![[]IBM](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/IBM_96x39.jpg)

[[]IBM](http://www.ibm.com/)

**Premier Sponsor**

**Social Event**

At IBM, we strive to lead in the creation, development and
manufacture of the industry's most advanced information technologies. IBM
has an application framework and provides an application server and
web design tools that give you the performance and flexibility you
want, to build the kind of web sites your companies and customers need.
IBM offers partnership programs that provide support and training
to help you get going - and growing - fast. IBM is e-business.

![[]Oracle](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/oracle_135x51.jpg)

[[]Oracle](http://www.oracle.com/)

**Premier Sponsor**

Oracle Corp. (Nasdaq: ORCL) provides the software that powers the
Internet. Headquartered in Redwood Shores, California, Oracle is the
first software company to develop and deploy 100% Internet-enabled
enterprise software across its entire product line: database,
application server, the e-Business Suite of enterprise business
applications, and application development and decision support tools. Oracle is
the only company capable of implementing complete global e-Business
enterprise solutions that extend from front office Customer
Relationship Management (CRM) to back office Enterprise Resource Planning
(ERP) applications to platform infrastructure. Oracle's World Wide
Web address is (URL) http://www.oracle.com/

![[]Sun Microsystems](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/sunlogo_135x80.gif)

[[]Sun Microsystems](http://www.sun.com/)

**Premier Sponsor**

**Internet Pavilion**

Since its inception in 1982, a singular vision - The Network Is The
Computer(tm) - has propelled Sun Microsystems, Inc. to its position
as a leading provider of industrial-strength hardware, software and
services that power the Internet and allow companies worldwide to
".com" their businesses. With $12.4 billion in annual revenues, Sun
can be found in more than 170 countries and at www.sun.com.

## ApacheCon Europe 2000's Corporate Sponsors

![[]Collab.Net](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/collab.net_135x49.jpg)

[[]Collab.Net](http://www.collab.net/)

**Delegate Portfolio and Pen**

Collab.Net is the provider of sourceXchange, a new Internet tool
that makes it easy for companies to sponsor Open Source projects that
address their specific concerns -- with guaranteed payment to the
developers who work on those projects. And this service is free for
developers!

![[]Fujitsu Siemens Computers](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/fujitsu-siemens_135x37.jpg)

[[]Fujitsu Siemens Computers](http://www.fujitsu-siemens.com/)

**Conference Proceedings Co-sponsor**

Fujitsu Siemens Computers is the leading European computer company
focussing on the benefits to the business needs. The efficient
support of Internet technology is the key prerequisite for using
BS2000/OSD Business Server as a high-end Internet Server. With Apache, the
OPEN GROUP organization has certified BS2000/OSD Business Server as
the world's first official Internet Server

## Other Sponsors of ApacheCon Europe 2000

![[]A.L. Digital and The Bunker](/images/events/apachecon-eu-2000/thebunker_135x54.gif)

